how to present your idea to big  companies I got a great question from  one of my youtube viewers love you guys  Bruce who wrote in to say he's an  inventor he's got a product he wants to  get it out there and he wants to partner  up with this big companies in his  industry and he wants my advice and how  to connect with them the right deal with  the right big company can make or break  a business right and so it's a it's a  great idea to be able to reach out to  these guys but how you do it is  important and a lot of people go about  it the wrong way and end up not getting  the deal that they want so I'm going to  give you three different ways to do it  in order of my preference from least  preferable to the most profitable the  first one is so number one reach out and  this is where you are contacting the  company directly you can find out who  the manager is in charge of the division  that's similar to what you're trying to  do and reach out to them or they may  have casting calls where they're looking  for inventors to come in and pitch their  products of them I remember this is how  I got in the salsa company I've invested  and we made a DVD and we went on the  Shopping Channel they had an open call  this anybody wants to pitch to us come  in and one of our buyers will talk to  you and so we pitched to them and we got  on the shopping channel that way so  sometimes there are these open calls or  you can just reach out to them reach out  to the person want to reach email phone  number and reach out the problem that I  have here the reason why I have a  problem with this and this is what most  people will do is because it gives you  no leverage right you're going to them  to say hey here's this great thing I  have check it out they have the power  and and that it bothers me it's hard  because there's no incentive motivation  reason for them to want to give you a  deal I give you a good deal because  you're going to them so here are two  other ways around it that can still work  but here are my two more preferred  preferred ways number two is partner up  and this is where you find someone who  already has a connection into that  business and you find a way to work  together maybe they represent you maybe  they introduce you but basically you  have somebody who's already done  business with them who they trust who  they like who they know and they say  this is a  a company who you have to check out and  so now it's not you on your hands and  knees begging please save me I'm this  inventor please save me but there's  someone who they respect and look up to  and trust saying hey this guy Bruce he  knows what he's doing you should connect  with him that's so much more powerful  put you more in the driving seat here's  an example I'm working on the book deal  and I have an agent and my agents out  there pitching to publishers they have  done a lot of work with my agent they  respect her they like her they trust her  when she says this is a good deal they  want to listen to her and so that puts  me in such a better position because now  I'm not going to the publisher and say  hey please mr. publisher do you want to  do a deal with me so find someone who's  already connected to that big company  and have them recommend you and make  that introduction the third one is build  momentum and create a movement this is  my favorite way to do it I don't even go  out anymore to talk to companies I have  them come to me and I've done deals with  some of the biggest companies in the  world Microsoft Dell Google banks tons  of companies have just found me because  they're looking to partner up with and  buy from people who are working with  entrepreneurs and if you're doing that  then you're going to come to me because  you see all the stuff that I put out  there so put out some similar stuff  build momentum for your business if you  look at companies that get acquired okay  that's a long-term goal for you if you  want to build a business or just sell  your idea but if you want to sell your  business look at how companies get  acquired it's rarely the company going  to the bigger company saying hey will  you please buy us we're desperate we  don't know where to go  we suck please buy us and save us right  it's not that kind of pitch it's usually  the big company seeing all the noise  that this little company has made and  saying we need to get this company we  need some of that here and they reach  out this is a scariest one because you  don't know who's watching you and you  don't know what kind of momentum that  you're actually building you may see a  little bit of results from customers and  social media but you don't know that big  company is watching you or not and you  have to  going trusting and believing that it's  going to work out even though you have  no idea what the end result is going to  be okay and that company that buys you  that company that you're in the  apartment what may not be the one  company that you had in mind this is  this is a huge problem that I had in my  business okay my first business one of  the biggest mistakes that I made okay  here this is it this is the goal we  wanted to partner up with a big company  we saw as being acquired by a big  company and we picked a company this is  a company that is going to buy us and we  worked for a whole summer on preparing a  presentation and how we're going to  pitch to them and we finally got in in a  room with them and they were interested  but because again I think us we went to  them we had no leverage they really  weren't too interested and ended up  being another company one of their  competitors that called us and said we  want to get into your space we're  interesting and maybe buying your  business or somebody else and we had to  do a 180 I start working on that deal  instead of the one that we spend all  this time working on we didn't expect  this deal to come out and they ended up  buying our competitor we were in the  final two but they bought our competitor  for almost a hundred million dollars  that was the deal I missed because I was  so focused on this one big company that  I didn't go off and think of other  opportunities and pay attention to the  momentum of building and that maybe  there are other people who are  interested in this so you're going to  have if you create a lot of you create a  storm  you create a movement you can start  creating momentum you're going to have a  lot of people interested in what you're  doing for a lot of different reasons and  the deal that you think you're going to  get is never the deal that you actually  get but it could be way better so those  are my three ways to reach out to big  companies and get your company off the  ground it's great that you're asking it  and start taking action don't get so  confused at all the options you don't do  anything that's the worst option of all  start moving forward and believe for  those of you watching like the video  please give it a thumbs up below let me  know what you think leave a comment  underneath subscribe to the channel  and I will see you guys soon
 

